 "head_commit": {
  "id": "6f2811d81f9ef16c2b044b016c5b369d7969ba4f",
  "tree_id": "2911b548ebd1c345abf35efbdfbeff792a3f993d",
  "message": "docs(reports): record the first complete native UCRT64 qualification\n\nWindows run 43456570072 at head 498d18d is the first full native qualification\nwith the owner's MSYS2 UCRT64 clang++: exact compiler path, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu,\nGNU ld 2.47.20260726, GNU libstdc++ 16.2.0, UCRT, SDL3 3.4.20-1 from the pinned\npackage, ImGui 1.93.0 compiled directly, Debug/Release builds, 15/15 native tests\nincluding a real Win32 window, selftest negatives, clean rebuild and a package that\nwas extracted and executed with a system-only PATH. Linux stayed green.\n\nUCRT64_WINDOWS_VALIDATION.md now contains those measured results, the honest skips\n(no ASan runtime in this UCRT64 clang, libFuzzer not accepted by clang's MinGW\ndriver, no interactive editor UI) and the requirement-by-requirement table.\nUCRT64_DEPENDENCIES.md records the observed package versions and the runtime DLL\nclosure with per-DLL package owners and digests. The evidence directory retains the\nannotations, run/job/artifact metadata, tree-identity proof, build-input digests\nand the real failing iterations that led here. Verbatim captured log excerpts keep\ntheir original trailing whitespace, as the earlier evidence directory does.\n\nThe doctor also keeps the compiler's own libFuzzer probe diagnostic now, so an\nunavailable capability always carries a measured reason.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>",
